{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"The mechanism is asserted as a causal 'Low-Pass Filter' but never specifies the physical process by which a checklist 'excises high-frequency signal.' To filter signal there must be a transformation that maps nuanced inputs to degraded outputs; SRC_001 instead restates the conclusion (ceiling on reliability) as a metaphor. It also provides no within-evaluation test that would distinguish a genuine reliability ceiling from a checklist that is simply not yet well-designed, so the causal story is unfalsifiable in a single evaluation.","target":"33fc72a7e3c89496cb3e3cd8e5dc7b97262ab0dc2398a80080f92e771a66ca00"},{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_002 invokes 'Error Cancellation' and 'Cognitive Redundancy' as labels, not as a causal mechanism. For statistical aggregation to yield error cancellation, the argument must show that errors are independent or at least not positively correlated; it merely lists groupthink as a countercondition without specifying the mechanism that produces independence or correction within a single evaluation. The claim that misreadings are 'outvoted or corrected' is asserted, not derived from any specified voting or correction process, so it cannot explain why the panel's distribution tightens around the truth rather than around a shared bias.","target":"384186ae96dd4cde663c4352655eaae8f5f0e7ee6366c41aa0d83b519d6ea87a"},{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_003 proposes 'Trace Analysis' as the distinguishing mechanism but provides no causal link from justification density to reliability. Citing specific evidence could itself become a compliance pattern (boilerplate with filler), and the only guard offered is a countercondition for 'faking'—not a mechanism that ties richer traces to better outcomes. Without specifying why denser traces cause higher accuracy, the proposal conflates a correlate of effort with a cause of reliability.","target":"76c31ff5835585ae535279aba9a1fee6901bdbfe87976fa245a9b5f9f7914e4f"}]}